    """
    value: ZIParameter[float, float]
    """Signal value written to the Aux Output port when Tip Protect is active. The value
    overwrites Aux Output Internal value and the Lower and Upper Limits.

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/TIPPROTECT/VALUE
    Properties: Read, Write, Setting
    Type: Double
    Unit: V
    """

class MFLIAuxouts(ZINode):
    """Node ``/DEV..../AUXOUTS/n``."""

    demodselect: ZIParameter[int, int]
    """Select the channel number of the selected signal source.

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/DEMODSELECT
    Properties: Read, Write, Setting
    Type: Integer (64 bit)
    """
    limitlower: ZIParameter[float, float]
    """Lower limit for the signal at the Auxiliary Output. A smaller value will be
    clipped.

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/LIMITLOWER
    Properties: Read, Write, Setting
    Type: Double
    Unit: V
    """
    limitupper: ZIParameter[float, float]
    """Upper limit for the signal at the Auxiliary Output. A larger value will be
    clipped.

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/LIMITUPPER
    Properties: Read, Write, Setting
    Type: Double
    Unit: V
    """
    max: ZIParameter[float, Never]
    """Indicates the maximum normalized voltage generated on this channel. It can be
    between -1 and 1. To prevent signal clipping and overvoltage, it is advised to
    keep it between -0.9 and 0.9.

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/MAX
    Properties: Read
    Type: Double
    """
    min: ZIParameter[float, Never]
    """Indicates the minimum normalized voltage generated on this channel. It can be
    between -1 and 1. To prevent signal clipping and overvoltage, it is advised to
    keep it between -0.9 and 0.9.

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/MIN
    Properties: Read
    Type: Double
    """
    offset: ZIParameter[float, float]
    """Add the specified offset voltage to the signal after scaling. Auxiliary Output
    Value = (Signal+Preoffset)*Scale + Offset

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/OFFSET
    Properties: Read, Write, Setting
    Type: Double
    Unit: V
    """
    outputselect: ZIParameter[int, int | str]
    """Select the signal source to be represented on the Auxiliary Output.

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/OUTPUTSELECT
    Properties: Read, Write, Setting
    Type: Integer (enumerated)

    Options:
        -1: "manual": Select Manual as the output option.
        0: "demod_x": Select Demod X as the output option.
        1: "demod_y": Select Demod Y as the output option.
        2: "demod_r": Select Demod R as the output option.
        3: "demod_theta": Select Demod Theta as the output option.
        5: "pid", "pid_out": Select PID Out as the output option.
        6: "boxcar": Select Boxcar as the output option.
        9: "pid_shift": Select PID Shift as the output option.
        10: "pid_error": Select PID Error as the output option.
        11: "tu_filtered": Select TU Filtered Value as the output option.
        13: "tu_output": Select TU Output Value as the output option.
    """
    preoffset: ZIParameter[float, float]
    """Add a pre-offset to the signal before scaling is applied. Auxiliary Output Value
    = (Signal+Preoffset)*Scale + Offset

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/PREOFFSET
    Properties: Read, Write, Setting
    Type: Double
    Unit: Dependent
    """
    scale: ZIParameter[float, float]
    """Multiplication factor to scale the signal. Auxiliary Output Value =
    (Signal+Preoffset)*Scale + Offset

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/SCALE
    Properties: Read, Write, Setting
    Type: Double
    """
    tipprotect: MFLIAuxoutsTipprotect
    value: ZIParameter[float, Never]
    """Voltage present on the Auxiliary Output. Auxiliary Output Value =
    (Signal+Preoffset)*Scale + Offset

    Node: /DEV..../AUXOUTS/n/VALUE
    Properties: Read
    Type: Double
    Unit: V
    """

class MFLIAuxinsValues(ZINode):
    """Node ``/DEV..../AUXINS/n/VALUES/n``."""

    value: ZIParameter[float, Never]
    """Voltage measured at the Auxiliary Input after averaging. The value of this node
    is updated at a low rate (50 Hz); the streaming node auxins/n/sample is updated
    at a high rate defined by the averaging.

    Node: /DEV..../AUXINS/n/VALUES/n
    Properties: Read
    Type: Double
    Unit: V
    """

class MFLIAuxins(ZINode):
    """Node ``/DEV..../AUXINS/n``."""

    averaging: ZIParameter[int, int]
    """Defines the number of samples on the input to average as a power of two. Possible
    values are in the range [0, 16]. A value of 0 corresponds to the sampling rate of
    the auxiliary input's ADC.

    Node: /DEV..../AUXINS/n/AVERAGING
    Properties: Read, Write, Setting
    Type: Integer (64 bit)
    """
    sample: ZIParameter[Any, Never]
    """Voltage measured at the Auxiliary Input after averaging. The data rate depends on
    the averaging value. Note, if the instrument has demodulator functionality, the
    auxiliary input values are available as fields in a demodulator sample and are
    aligned by timestamp with the demodulator output.

    Node: /DEV..../AUXINS/n/SAMPLE
    Properties: Read, Stream
    Type: ZIAuxInSample
    Unit: V
    """
    values: ZIChannelList[MFLIAuxinsValues]

class MFLINodes:
    """Node tree of the MFLI."""

    auxins: ZIChannelList[MFLIAuxins]
